WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.470 --> 00:06.470
So you're going to take me every day?

3
00:06.470 --> 00:08.800
If you don't mind the hassle, I'd like to.

4
00:08.800 --> 00:11.670
Then next time you come, wait inside the house.

5
00:11.670 --> 00:13.030
Don't stand out in the sun.

6
00:13.670 --> 00:14.870
What are you doing, Din?

7
00:14.870 --> 00:17.330
I just wanted to try guessing.

8
00:17.330 --> 00:19.530
But when you said you didn't want to see me,

9
00:19.530 --> 00:20.870
I was lost.

10
00:20.870 --> 00:21.930
You should go, Physics.

11
00:21.930 --> 00:25.100
I can't imagine what I'd be without you.

12
00:25.100 --> 00:25.970
I like you, Physics.

13
00:25.970 --> 00:27.100
Come to England with me.

14
00:27.100 --> 00:28.670
Well, every plan in my life...

15
00:28.670 --> 00:30.230
has always had you in it.

16
00:30.230 --> 00:32.170
I don't know how to tell my parents.

17
00:32.170 --> 00:34.000
Rei, you fucker. What about the baby?

18
00:34.000 --> 00:35.600
Huh? That's your kid, asshole.

19
00:35.600 --> 00:38.530
This is between me and Mii. Stay the fuck out of it.

20
00:38.530 --> 00:39.800
Then tell me, Mii,

21
00:39.800 --> 00:41.230
what you want me to do.

22
00:41.230 --> 00:42.800
Fine. I'll tell you.

23
00:42.800 --> 00:44.470
Get out of my life.

24
00:44.470 --> 00:47.800
Do you know your words and your actions don't match?

25
00:47.800 --> 00:50.430
You say you didn't mean to leave me,

26
00:50.430 --> 00:51.430
but you did.

27
00:51.430 --> 00:54.000
My friend was in trouble. I couldn't leave my friend.

28
00:54.000 --> 00:55.200
Couldn't leave your friend.

29
00:55.800 --> 00:57.070
But you could leave me.

30
00:57.070 --> 00:58.730
I can't trust you anymore.

31
00:58.730 --> 00:59.700
I've had enough

32
00:59.700 --> 01:01.300
of everything about you.

33
01:01.300 --> 01:02.530
This is my last warning.

34
01:02.530 --> 01:03.600
Leave my brother alone.

35
01:04.129 --> 01:05.300
Physics, but...

36
01:05.300 --> 01:07.000
Hey! Physics!

37
01:07.000 --> 01:09.330
You can hit me as many times as you want.

38
01:09.930 --> 01:11.630
But can't you give me a chance?

39
01:19.000 --> 01:20.800
Oh, hello. / Hello.

40
01:21.530 --> 01:24.030
Oh, bye-bye.

41
01:31.430 --> 01:32.470
Hey!

42
01:41.000 --> 01:42.330
Let me help pick them up.

43
01:43.570 --> 01:44.930
It's okay.

44
01:58.600 --> 01:59.970
Din!

45
01:59.970 --> 02:02.770
Star, what's wrong this time?

46
02:06.170 --> 02:07.730
What happened in there?

47
02:08.030 --> 02:09.570
Din, let's just go.

48
02:09.570 --> 02:11.000
I'll tell you later.

49
04:05.000 --> 04:07.270
Why didn't you tell me sooner, Star?

50
04:07.870 --> 04:09.700
It's really dangerous, you know?

51
04:13.400 --> 04:15.100
I'm sorry, Din.

52
04:15.570 --> 04:17.829
I thought he was just messing around.

53
04:18.570 --> 04:21.200
And nothing like this has happened in a long time.

54
04:21.200 --> 04:23.570
I think we should tell your dad about this.

55
04:23.570 --> 04:25.500
So he can help if anything happens.

56
04:25.500 --> 04:27.030
Please don't, Din.

57
04:27.600 --> 04:30.470
If you tell my dad, it'll turn into a big deal.

58
04:30.470 --> 04:32.030
But... / Please.

59
04:33.370 --> 04:34.870
I'll change my class time

60
04:34.870 --> 04:36.900
or switch rooms.

61
04:36.900 --> 04:39.330
So no one has to worry.

62
04:39.930 --> 04:41.470
Please, Din.

63
04:48.170 --> 04:51.400
Then from now on, I'll take you to class every day

64
04:51.400 --> 04:53.270
and wait to pick you up, too.

65
04:55.630 --> 04:57.230
Thank you.

66
04:58.370 --> 04:59.570
Hungry?

67
05:01.670 --> 05:03.200
A little.

68
05:03.770 --> 05:06.170
Then eat something to take your mind off it.

69
05:08.770 --> 05:10.900
Are you really okay, Din?

70
05:12.930 --> 05:14.870
I'm okay with the food.

71
05:14.870 --> 05:17.070
But I'm not okay with what happened.

72
05:25.870 --> 05:27.800
It's fine. Eat up.

73
05:39.830 --> 05:44.270
Star, I'll be right here with you.

74
05:48.300 --> 05:50.330
Thank you, Din.

75
06:14.630 --> 06:15.970
Ooh! / Hey!

76
06:15.970 --> 06:17.270
Why'd you hit me?

77
06:26.230 --> 06:28.270
Is this yours? / Hm.

78
06:30.430 --> 06:34.770
Brot you some snaks. Enjoy.

79
06:35.130 --> 06:36.800
Where do you think he's from?

80
06:36.800 --> 06:38.900
Not from Bangkok, I bet.

81
06:56.870 --> 06:58.900
You think it's him, right?

82
06:58.900 --> 07:02.000
You-know-who.

83
07:03.530 --> 07:06.070
Mm, that's him.

84
07:07.200 --> 07:10.800
Do you think we're like dogs or what?

85
07:14.700 --> 07:18.530
Let him do whatever he wants. Don't worry about me.

86
07:18.530 --> 07:20.700
I don't want to go back anymore.

87
07:24.730 --> 07:26.730
Here, eat up. / For real?

88
07:27.030 --> 07:29.570
It'll all be gone by evening. / Just take it.

89
07:29.830 --> 07:31.070
Thanks, bro.

90
07:47.300 --> 07:49.570
Oh, gather up! We're done!

91
07:51.500 --> 07:53.670
Sit, sit, sit.

92
07:57.130 --> 07:58.730
The real match is soon.

93
08:00.170 --> 08:03.030
So get plenty of rest these days.

94
08:03.530 --> 08:06.170
As for the M.6 students taking university exams,

95
08:06.170 --> 08:08.730
don't push yourselves too hard training.

96
08:09.730 --> 08:12.430
Go on, we're done! Go home and rest!

97
08:13.830 --> 08:15.770
See you, everyone. Thank you.

98
08:15.770 --> 08:16.870
See ya.

99
08:17.770 --> 08:19.770
Go home. / See you, man.

100
08:23.200 --> 08:24.870
Thanop, see ya. / Get home safe.

101
08:26.070 --> 08:27.830
See ya, man. / Bye, sir.

102
08:28.130 --> 08:30.300
Coach, can you stay a bit longer? / What?

103
08:30.300 --> 08:33.500
Can you stay and help me practice shooting?

104
08:33.500 --> 08:35.200
At this hour? / Yes.

105
08:35.330 --> 08:36.169
Oh, well.

106
08:36.169 --> 08:38.870
Jay, are you in a hurry to get home?

107
08:39.030 --> 08:39.630
Hm?

108
08:40.500 --> 08:41.630
Go play keeper for me.

109
08:42.730 --> 08:44.270
Me? / Yeah.

110
08:47.030 --> 08:48.130
Fine, just for a bit.

111
08:48.130 --> 08:49.770
Go on, just for a bit.

112
08:49.770 --> 08:50.930
Shooting practice.

113
08:50.930 --> 08:53.100
The most important thing in shooting

114
08:53.100 --> 08:54.370
is a solid stance.

115
08:54.970 --> 08:56.630
You're hot-headed.

116
08:56.630 --> 08:59.870
You need to stay calm and look at the goal.

117
08:59.870 --> 09:03.200
Think of the goal as your target,

118
09:03.200 --> 09:06.200
the future you have to step into.

119
09:06.200 --> 09:08.730
The moment you see an opening, shoot.

120
10:16.830 --> 10:18.170
Hello, Mii.

121
10:18.170 --> 10:20.270
Aof, I talked to my parents.

122
10:20.270 --> 10:24.470
Honestly, I feel so relieved. They scolded me a bit.

123
10:24.470 --> 10:27.370
But at least I don't have to deal with it alone.

124
10:27.370 --> 10:29.300
Mm, good.

125
10:29.300 --> 10:31.130
So are you going anywhere today?

126
10:31.130 --> 10:33.930
I'm going to the hospital with my dad.

127
10:33.930 --> 10:36.100
And once everything's done,

128
10:36.100 --> 10:37.600
I'm taking the little one

129
10:37.600 --> 10:40.070
to Australia to raise it with my aunt.

130
10:41.500 --> 10:43.100
Don't be reckless, Mii.

131
10:43.100 --> 10:44.800
Or the little one might get hurt.

132
10:44.800 --> 10:49.500
Don't worry, Aof. I'm fine. Thank you, dear Aof.

133
11:12.270 --> 11:13.100
Mom.

134
11:14.030 --> 11:16.870
Isn't this way too much?

135
11:16.870 --> 11:19.130
This could feed the whole neighborhood.

136
11:19.970 --> 11:21.300
It's not too much.

137
11:21.300 --> 11:24.370
I'll hand some out to the neighbors and it'll be gone.

138
11:24.830 --> 11:26.500
See, the whole neighborhood.

139
11:27.100 --> 11:30.300
Oh, take some over to Fuen's place, too.

140
11:31.200 --> 11:32.730
Sure, Mom.

141
11:35.970 --> 11:39.630
Did you accept the UK university's offer yet?

142
11:39.970 --> 11:43.000
The university... Oh, I've accepted.

143
11:43.000 --> 11:45.830
I just got the confirmation email this morning.

144
11:47.130 --> 11:52.770
And Fuen agreed to go to England with you, right?

145
11:54.830 --> 11:56.330
Yes.

146
11:56.330 --> 11:59.830
Great. I'll look for a language course for him.

147
11:59.830 --> 12:02.500
Oh, sure. Sure.

148
12:03.500 --> 12:04.700
And what about you?

149
12:05.530 --> 12:08.170
Want to take a fun class over the break?

150
12:08.170 --> 12:09.730
How about languages?

151
12:11.130 --> 12:13.200
Maybe not languages yet, bro.

152
12:14.000 --> 12:19.000
But... can I take singing lessons?

153
12:21.330 --> 12:24.970
Please, Mom, I really want to learn.

154
12:27.900 --> 12:29.670
Okay, okay. Fine.

155
12:30.400 --> 12:34.130
Go find what you want to learn, where, and with who. / Okay.

156
12:34.130 --> 12:35.630
Show it to me first.

157
12:35.630 --> 12:37.100
Or should I find one for you?

158
12:37.500 --> 12:39.330
No, I'm good.

159
12:39.670 --> 12:43.300
Last time, I had you learn country music.

160
12:43.300 --> 12:44.700
With Kru Sala, no less.

161
12:45.530 --> 12:48.370
Okay, okay, go find one and show me. Okay?

162
12:48.370 --> 12:49.870
Okay.

163
12:49.870 --> 12:51.670
Thank you, Mom.

164
12:55.430 --> 12:58.370
Just study hard. That's all I need.

165
12:58.370 --> 12:59.530
Yes, dear. / Okay.

166
12:59.530 --> 13:00.830
Okay, sweetie? / Sure.

167
13:00.830 --> 13:03.230
Let's get back to it. I'll take some to Fuen.

168
13:03.900 --> 13:04.930
Done yet?

169
13:04.930 --> 13:06.030
Been at it a while.

170
13:18.830 --> 13:21.100
You're really not taking the med exam?

171
13:22.970 --> 13:25.100
Let me be stubborn about this one, Mom.

172
13:30.030 --> 13:31.670
Engineering it is, then.

173
13:31.670 --> 13:34.300
If you think you can do it, it's your call.

174
13:35.670 --> 13:36.700
Thank you.

175
13:36.700 --> 13:38.170
Are you going anywhere later?

176
13:38.170 --> 13:40.030
I'm meeting a friend tonight, Mom.

177
13:40.030 --> 13:41.700
Oh my, are you seeing someone?

178
13:41.700 --> 13:43.770
Hey, not yet.

179
13:43.770 --> 13:47.700
Don't date yet. Focus on university for now, understand?

180
13:48.170 --> 13:49.770
I'm heading out in a bit.

181
13:49.770 --> 13:52.030
I'm meeting Auntie Pat, okay?

182
13:52.030 --> 13:53.100
Okay.

183
14:11.370 --> 14:13.200
You haven't left yet, Mom?

184
14:16.700 --> 14:18.130
Did you forget something?

185
14:25.530 --> 14:28.630
Din, I need your advice on something.

186
14:29.130 --> 14:30.900
Can I come in?

187
14:44.470 --> 14:46.700
Have you talked to Physics about this?

188
14:48.630 --> 14:49.700
Not yet.

189
14:50.700 --> 14:52.400
If he knows I'm stressed,

190
14:52.400 --> 14:54.130
he'll overthink it again.

191
14:55.600 --> 14:58.600
But you should tell him what you're thinking.

192
14:58.900 --> 15:01.370
But I don't know where to start.

193
15:02.630 --> 15:05.070
Physics has helped me so much.

194
15:05.070 --> 15:06.500
Taking me to classes,

195
15:06.500 --> 15:08.500
tutoring me on the side.

196
15:08.500 --> 15:10.870
His family supports me all the way, too.

197
15:11.800 --> 15:13.030
That's why I'm scared.

198
15:13.730 --> 15:15.630
Because if I don't get in,

199
15:15.630 --> 15:17.830
he'll start thinking crazy things again.

200
15:25.070 --> 15:28.370
That day, he showed me a bunch of universities.

201
15:28.830 --> 15:30.970
There was one I really liked,

202
15:31.570 --> 15:33.600
but it's not in London.

203
15:34.200 --> 15:36.000
And the one that is in London,

204
15:36.470 --> 15:39.630
I don't think I'll get in this year.

205
15:42.230 --> 15:43.670
So what do you think, Fuen?

206
15:44.330 --> 15:47.430
Study together, or somewhere else?

207
15:48.000 --> 15:52.000
Honestly, they're both Architecture.

208
15:52.530 --> 15:54.170
Anywhere is fine.

209
15:55.370 --> 15:59.770
But if we're going together, the same city is easier.

210
16:03.730 --> 16:07.600
I haven't even told my parents I'm going.

211
16:07.600 --> 16:09.270
Then tell them first.

212
16:10.130 --> 16:12.600
And for art programs,

213
16:12.600 --> 16:15.130
you need a portfolio, right? Have you made one?

214
16:15.130 --> 16:18.170
Did you keep the stuff you used to draw for fun?

215
16:19.170 --> 16:21.930
I have some, but it's all over the place.

216
16:22.600 --> 16:24.200
I just draw whatever.

217
16:25.570 --> 16:28.670
But I kept the designs I helped my dad with.

218
16:28.670 --> 16:31.430
That's fine. They just need to be in the same group.

219
16:32.030 --> 16:35.730
And when you're free, go check out the seniors' work at uni.

220
16:35.730 --> 16:39.670
Like open houses or thesis shows.

221
16:40.070 --> 16:45.070
Man, coming to you was the right call. Thanks a lot.

222
16:45.930 --> 16:48.830
And you're applying with a portfolio too, right?

223
16:49.730 --> 16:50.730
Mm.

224
16:51.230 --> 16:53.030
But not for med school.

225
16:53.430 --> 16:54.430
Hey!

226
16:55.830 --> 16:57.300
I still want engineering.

227
16:57.300 --> 16:58.600
Mm.

228
16:58.600 --> 17:01.470
My mom's a little sulky about it, too.

229
17:01.470 --> 17:02.870
But she didn't say anything.

230
17:03.700 --> 17:05.329
What's there to say?

231
17:05.329 --> 17:08.430
You'll get in somewhere. I'm not worried about you.

232
17:08.430 --> 17:10.000
Worry about me.

233
17:10.970 --> 17:12.800
Let's hope so.

234
17:14.099 --> 17:17.730
Thanks a lot. I'm off, then. Thank you.

235
17:54.600 --> 17:56.500
Say whatever it is.

236
18:05.700 --> 18:08.100
Dad, Mom...

237
18:12.100 --> 18:15.230
Can I go study abroad with Physics?

238
18:24.200 --> 18:25.800
Son,

239
18:27.130 --> 18:29.970
your English is still a disaster.

240
18:32.630 --> 18:34.600
Let me ask you something.

241
18:34.600 --> 18:38.400
Do you want to go because you really want to study?

242
18:38.770 --> 18:40.900
Or because of Physics?

243
18:42.500 --> 18:46.170
At first it was because of him. Now it's both.

244
18:46.170 --> 18:48.670
I'm working really hard at my tutoring classes.

245
18:48.670 --> 18:51.570
And Physics's mom is helping me with a lot of things.

246
18:51.900 --> 18:57.500
Dad, Mom, I don't know if I'll get in.

247
18:57.500 --> 18:59.470
But I'm trying.

248
19:04.470 --> 19:05.730
Fuen, sweetie.

249
19:06.400 --> 19:12.370
If you don't get in, that's okay. We'll do a course.

250
19:12.370 --> 19:16.400
You don't mind if I don't graduate with everyone else?

251
19:16.400 --> 19:21.430
Son, your dad and I are ready to support you.

252
19:21.430 --> 19:24.530
We'll pay for your studies, for your dream,

253
19:24.530 --> 19:26.670
for your happiness, my son.

254
19:27.300 --> 19:32.500
Fuen, listen to me. I'm being serious.

255
19:36.500 --> 19:38.630
Since you're running off together,

256
19:40.130 --> 19:43.030
tell his parents to come ask properly.

257
19:43.030 --> 19:44.070
Dad!

258
19:45.430 --> 19:47.030
Brilliant, honey.

259
19:47.330 --> 19:48.730
Oh, you too, Mom?

260
19:48.730 --> 19:50.600
Most brilliant idea ever, honey.

261
19:53.630 --> 19:55.670
I was worried sick before asking.

262
19:58.400 --> 19:59.900
That's all it took, son.

263
20:16.870 --> 20:19.170
Meet me here after class.

264
20:19.170 --> 20:21.800
Oh, won't you get bored?

265
20:21.800 --> 20:24.100
My class is two whole hours.

266
20:27.130 --> 20:30.170
Don't worry. I've got stuff to do while I wait.

267
20:30.170 --> 20:31.300
Go on to class.

268
20:31.300 --> 20:32.770
Okay.

269
20:35.830 --> 20:36.830
Star!

270
20:37.530 --> 20:38.530
Yeah?

271
20:40.030 --> 20:42.630
Focus on class. Don't worry.

272
21:17.170 --> 21:19.700
You can stop trying to guess.

273
21:19.700 --> 21:21.470
Even if you get some letters right,

274
21:21.470 --> 21:25.100
you'll never guess the last three.

275
21:26.100 --> 21:27.670
Is it that obvious on my face?

276
21:34.870 --> 21:39.670
I'm off to class, then, Guardian Din.

277
21:51.300 --> 21:53.370
Is my face really that obvious?

278
22:06.300 --> 22:07.700
What are you reading?

279
22:09.630 --> 22:15.600
Oh, I'm looking at the university you want to get into.

280
22:15.600 --> 22:17.770
What exams you need.

281
22:22.800 --> 22:26.100
As far as I remember, for your IELTS,

282
22:26.100 --> 22:30.730
you need around 5.5 to 6.5, depending on the program.

283
22:32.230 --> 22:33.670
Whoa.

284
22:33.670 --> 22:37.500
And these are the A-Levels you need for admission.

285
22:40.500 --> 22:42.870
No room for me falling short, huh?

286
22:46.000 --> 22:49.470
I don't want to pressure you.

287
22:51.570 --> 22:54.100
Or if you don't get in this year,

288
22:54.100 --> 22:57.230
why not take a language course for a year?

289
22:57.870 --> 23:01.600
Hey, don't lower your expectations yet.

290
23:02.300 --> 23:08.770
Aim for the university first. If it fails, we'll see.

291
23:16.670 --> 23:18.470
Tired?

292
23:21.870 --> 23:25.330
Tired... but I'm not giving up.

293
23:39.200 --> 23:41.530
Thanks for trying so hard for me.

294
24:13.670 --> 24:14.830
Din!

295
24:18.170 --> 24:20.570
I told you I'd wait right here.

296
24:24.800 --> 24:26.630
Come on, let's go home.

297
24:37.370 --> 24:40.530
Din, um...

298
24:41.270 --> 24:43.800
Can I ask you something personal?

299
24:43.800 --> 24:47.130
Mm, sure. What do you want to know?

300
24:48.700 --> 24:53.470
You and Yok... are you two still...

301
25:05.670 --> 25:07.500
We're not anything anymore.

302
25:08.470 --> 25:11.730
At most, we're just acquaintances.

303
25:14.700 --> 25:17.870
If you want to know anything else, just ask me.

304
25:17.870 --> 25:19.830
I'll answer everything.

305
25:22.000 --> 25:23.100
Okay.

306
25:24.130 --> 25:25.670
That's all.

307
25:27.170 --> 25:30.400
But are you in a hurry this evening?

308
25:31.730 --> 25:34.430
My dad's inviting you to dinner.

309
25:36.670 --> 25:39.000
And he specifically said

310
25:39.000 --> 25:40.900
you have to come.

311
25:40.900 --> 25:42.100
Your dad...

312
25:42.730 --> 25:44.630
Your dad's inviting me to dinner?

313
25:45.370 --> 25:46.930
Yes.

314
25:48.200 --> 25:50.500
Shall we hurry, then?

315
25:50.500 --> 25:53.530
My dad's really strict, Din.

316
25:53.530 --> 25:55.530
Let's go, let's go eat!

317
26:09.900 --> 26:13.070
Come, eat. I made plenty.

318
26:13.500 --> 26:15.930
Here, take the shrimp first.

319
26:15.930 --> 26:17.770
You're good at peeling, huh?

320
26:19.470 --> 26:20.300
Yeah.

321
26:20.800 --> 26:22.430
So, Din,

322
26:22.670 --> 26:25.970
your exams are coming up. Studying hard?

323
26:25.970 --> 26:27.270
Pretty much.

324
26:27.270 --> 26:29.070
But I'll try the portfolio round first.

325
26:29.070 --> 26:30.800
If I get in, I'll just take it.

326
26:30.800 --> 26:32.730
Mm, good idea.

327
26:32.730 --> 26:35.330
Is it a university you already like?

328
26:35.330 --> 26:37.800
Yes. I looked at the curriculum and loved it.

329
26:37.800 --> 26:40.570
I think studying there would be fun.

330
26:40.570 --> 26:44.900
Mm, good. Study somewhere you like.

331
26:45.430 --> 26:48.070
And do you think first year will be tough?

332
26:49.730 --> 26:51.770
I'm not sure.

333
26:52.530 --> 26:53.600
Star!

334
26:54.030 --> 26:55.700
He'll be studying hard,

335
26:56.230 --> 26:58.330
so no whining, got it?

336
26:59.000 --> 27:00.530
Dad!

337
27:02.400 --> 27:05.470
Din, peel some shrimp for me too, son.

338
27:11.470 --> 27:14.030
Here you go, sir. All peeled.

339
27:15.030 --> 27:17.470
As skilled as they say.

340
27:53.670 --> 27:55.200
Homework. I'll hand it in.

341
27:55.200 --> 27:56.730
Oh, yeah.

342
28:01.130 --> 28:02.300
Thank you.

343
28:47.130 --> 28:48.230
What?

344
28:48.570 --> 28:51.400
I'm glad to see you working hard at something.

345
28:51.800 --> 28:54.530
But take a break. Too much isn't good.

346
28:55.000 --> 28:57.570
But you know, if I can't pull it off this time...

347
29:00.070 --> 29:01.400
Don't think like that.

348
29:01.400 --> 29:02.800
You can do it.

349
29:03.370 --> 29:05.470
Just stay as cocky as usual.

350
29:06.200 --> 29:08.500
Tang, are you insulting me?

351
29:09.630 --> 29:10.630
Isn't it wet?

352
29:11.870 --> 29:14.170
Oh, I'll probably be late on match day.

353
29:14.170 --> 29:15.730
I'm going to an open house first.

354
29:15.730 --> 29:16.970
Up to you.

355
29:17.530 --> 29:19.200
Honestly, you don't have to come.

356
29:19.430 --> 29:21.570
You're not that important to me anyway.

357
29:22.800 --> 29:26.870
But you're a footballer. Why are you swimming?

358
29:27.700 --> 29:29.970
You never really get me, do you?

359
29:30.300 --> 29:33.070
I swim so my lungs get stronger.

360
29:33.500 --> 29:35.830
So I can run all day, morning to night.

361
29:36.630 --> 29:37.970
Get it?

362
29:39.370 --> 29:41.070
Talking to you is a waste of time.

363
29:41.070 --> 29:42.930
I'm going back to swimming.

364
29:52.070 --> 29:54.170
Who the hell could understand you?

365
29:54.800 --> 29:57.770
Your brain's gone to mush.

366
30:07.330 --> 30:11.170
Number 14, Aof, has really grown up, Coach.

367
30:11.900 --> 30:13.130
You think so, sir?

368
30:13.130 --> 30:14.130
Yeah.

369
30:27.070 --> 30:29.030
Come on! Woo!

370
30:29.030 --> 30:31.070
I think so too.

371
30:51.000 --> 30:52.500
Probably needs to poop.

372
30:52.500 --> 30:54.930
Players always need to poop after scoring.

373
30:54.930 --> 30:56.000
Happens to me a lot.

374
30:56.330 --> 30:58.970
So Ronaldo would be pooping all match?

375
30:58.970 --> 31:01.000
Keep practicing, come on!

376
31:02.100 --> 31:03.170
Physics!

377
31:04.100 --> 31:05.700
You came to watch me?

378
31:08.570 --> 31:11.470
Just stopped by to watch you play.

379
31:13.000 --> 31:17.430
So what's your next plan?

380
31:18.200 --> 31:21.530
You sneak my brother home every day.

381
31:21.530 --> 31:23.230
You think I don't know?

382
31:25.430 --> 31:27.300
You knew?

383
31:27.630 --> 31:28.730
Mm.

384
31:29.630 --> 31:31.270
My mom knows, too.

385
31:33.800 --> 31:36.470
How long are you going to avoid looking at me?

386
31:36.470 --> 31:39.170
I'm not your dad. I'm your friend.

387
31:45.900 --> 31:47.100
Not talking? I'm leaving.

388
31:47.100 --> 31:47.900
Physics!

389
31:48.870 --> 31:50.000
Um...

390
31:53.400 --> 31:55.970
Just you not stopping me makes me really happy.

391
32:11.400 --> 32:13.870
The reason I never gave you a chance

392
32:14.830 --> 32:16.070
is you being an ass.

393
32:17.470 --> 32:18.900
And you're all talk,

394
32:18.900 --> 32:20.570
you never really show it.

395
32:20.900 --> 32:25.570
But this time, you're proving it to everyone around you.

396
32:25.570 --> 32:26.730
Not just me.

397
32:29.670 --> 32:30.730
Well?

398
32:30.730 --> 32:32.030
You gonna stay quiet?

399
32:34.500 --> 32:36.430
Well? Are you going to ask?

400
32:39.070 --> 32:41.330
Then let me court your brother again, Physics.

401
32:41.330 --> 32:42.530
Physics, I'm begging you.

402
32:42.530 --> 32:44.270
Okay, okay, you can. / Really?

403
32:45.230 --> 32:46.100
Yes, you can!

404
32:46.470 --> 32:49.300
But I won't if you keep messing around like this.

405
32:49.300 --> 32:50.570
Okay, okay, okay.

406
32:51.100 --> 32:52.600
I give up, I give up.

407
32:58.470 --> 32:59.800
Fine, I'll allow it.

408
33:00.900 --> 33:02.870
But don't hurt my brother again.

409
33:02.870 --> 33:03.870
Got it.

410
33:04.100 --> 33:06.630
Make him cry again and you'll get it again.

411
33:09.000 --> 33:12.530
But whether Chemi lets you court him, you'll have to ask him.

412
33:13.600 --> 33:15.900
That's all I can do as his brother.

413
33:16.470 --> 33:18.830
Mm, I love you, Physics. Thanks so much.

414
33:18.830 --> 33:20.130
Hey, go practice.

415
33:20.130 --> 33:20.770
True friend.

416
33:20.770 --> 33:24.470
Give me a kiss. Physics, Physics, give me a kiss.

417
33:34.500 --> 33:37.830
One, two, three... Yay!

418
33:38.700 --> 33:39.700
Chemi!

419
33:46.230 --> 33:48.230
Can I talk to you for a moment?

420
33:50.370 --> 33:52.030
Just a minute.

421
33:57.030 --> 33:59.000
If there's something, just say it.

422
34:01.530 --> 34:03.430
I've got a big match this Sunday.

423
34:04.170 --> 34:05.630
Will you come watch me?

424
34:08.900 --> 34:10.130
I'm busy.

425
34:16.070 --> 34:18.130
Is that all you wanted to say?

426
34:18.400 --> 34:19.800
I understand

427
34:21.000 --> 34:23.630
that you won't forgive me.

428
34:24.030 --> 34:26.530
But can I have one more chance?

429
34:26.530 --> 34:28.500
Even if it's the last one.

430
34:29.800 --> 34:32.570
I want you to see that I've really changed.

431
34:40.670 --> 34:41.900
I told you,

432
34:42.400 --> 34:44.570
I don't want anything from you anymore.

433
34:45.130 --> 34:46.600
Stop forcing yourself.

434
34:46.600 --> 34:48.400
I'm not forcing anything.

435
34:50.500 --> 34:52.330
Today I realized...

436
34:53.000 --> 34:55.630
not thinking things through ruined everything.

437
34:56.600 --> 35:00.870
I kept making excuses so you'd forgive me like always.

438
35:01.300 --> 35:02.700
But now I get it.

439
35:02.700 --> 35:04.730
What I should do is apologize to you,

440
35:05.300 --> 35:07.400
and finally do what I say.

441
35:11.200 --> 35:13.170
Will you give me one more chance?

442
35:13.470 --> 35:14.930
Even if it's the last one.

443
35:16.030 --> 35:18.400
I promise, if I ruin it again this time,

444
35:18.830 --> 35:20.830
you'll never see my face again.

445
35:21.670 --> 35:26.330
♪ There's something in my heart I can't explain ♪

446
35:26.330 --> 35:30.670
♪ Still searching for someone to tell me ♪

447
35:30.670 --> 35:34.100
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

448
35:34.100 --> 35:36.300
♪ I never find what I'm looking for ♪

449
35:36.300 --> 35:41.000
♪ Why does my heart still feel so empty? ♪

450
35:46.830 --> 35:47.830
Mm.

451
35:49.100 --> 35:50.800
So what are you going to do?

452
35:51.200 --> 35:52.930
At the match this Sunday,

453
35:52.930 --> 35:54.930
I'll score five goals on my own.

454
35:54.930 --> 35:56.430
If I do...

455
35:56.800 --> 35:58.900
will you say yes?

456
35:58.900 --> 36:00.330
But if I don't,

457
36:00.330 --> 36:03.270
I promise you'll never see my face again.

458
36:16.100 --> 36:20.700
Up to you. But if you can't do it...

459
36:20.700 --> 36:22.900
please keep your promise

460
36:23.800 --> 36:25.900
that I'll never see you again.

461
36:34.400 --> 36:37.630
Okay, Chemi. I promise!

462
36:39.800 --> 36:45.400
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

463
36:45.400 --> 36:52.270
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

464
37:12.730 --> 37:18.470
"You going with me tomorrow?"

465
37:23.930 --> 37:27.200
"I want to go a bit later."

466
37:27.200 --> 37:30.100
"I'll catch up."

467
37:30.100 --> 37:34.370
"Okay. Call me when you get there. I'll come get you."

468
37:42.570 --> 37:44.070
Thank you.

469
37:51.900 --> 37:53.170
We have to register today?

470
37:53.170 --> 37:55.230
Yeah. You haven't yet? / Not yet.

471
37:55.230 --> 37:56.830
The whole class has registered.

472
37:56.830 --> 37:58.470
If you don't register today,

473
37:58.470 --> 38:00.170
might have to wait till next year.

474
38:00.170 --> 38:01.470
Next year?

475
38:55.130 --> 38:57.530
"Dude, you coming to watch my match?"

476
39:03.070 --> 39:05.300
"I'll see."

477
39:06.700 --> 39:10.800
♪ When you said I was too young ♪

478
39:10.800 --> 39:18.900
♪ But it's okay, I'll still wait until that day ♪

479
39:18.900 --> 39:24.670
♪ The day you're here with me ♪

480
39:25.630 --> 39:30.800
♪ No matter how long it takes, my heart still calls for you ♪

481
39:30.800 --> 39:37.430
♪ Because this heart of mine is still waiting, only for you ♪

482
40:53.830 --> 40:55.330
What's on your mind?

483
40:56.300 --> 40:59.700
Thanop... today I want five goals on my own.

484
40:59.700 --> 41:03.300
Why five? Just winning the game is enough.

485
41:04.500 --> 41:06.430
I have to score five goals today

486
41:06.430 --> 41:08.700
to get another chance with Chemi.

487
41:10.100 --> 41:12.470
And you're betting it all on a match?

488
41:12.500 --> 41:13.870
Can you even handle it?

489
41:13.870 --> 41:15.900
I don't have any other choice.

490
41:16.830 --> 41:19.330
Football's the only thing I'm good at.

491
41:19.570 --> 41:21.330
If it were one of our past matches,

492
41:21.330 --> 41:23.230
I'd say we had a shot.

493
41:23.230 --> 41:27.130
But today we're up against Rei. Suan Mali.

494
41:28.330 --> 41:30.400
I have to pull it off, no matter what.

495
41:34.130 --> 41:36.170
Help me out, Thanop.

496
41:36.970 --> 41:39.100
You can't just ask me.

497
41:39.430 --> 41:41.170
Go tell the whole team.

498
41:53.530 --> 41:55.530
You sure know how to cause me trouble.

499
41:55.530 --> 41:58.370
So I have to plan for you to score alone, Aof?

500
41:58.400 --> 41:59.600
Huh?

501
41:59.600 --> 42:02.600
Well... yes, Coach.

502
42:03.100 --> 42:05.600
Aof, I can't let you do that.

503
42:05.600 --> 42:07.830
Or you'll be their target all game.

504
42:08.730 --> 42:09.870
Coach...

505
42:09.900 --> 42:11.470
What gives, Thanop?

506
42:11.470 --> 42:13.200
I send you to talk to him once,

507
42:13.200 --> 42:15.370
and you lose your head along with him?

508
42:15.400 --> 42:17.770
I really can't do that.

509
42:17.770 --> 42:19.700
Because if the team loses,

510
42:19.700 --> 42:22.470
all our training goes to waste. You know that?

511
42:22.470 --> 42:25.600
Yes. But no matter what, I have to win today.

512
42:26.070 --> 42:28.200
And I'll score five goals on my own.

513
42:28.200 --> 42:31.200
Coach, he's rarely this fired up.

514
42:31.200 --> 42:33.170
Coach, why not give him a shot?

515
42:46.670 --> 42:49.330
I can't decide this alone.

516
42:49.830 --> 42:50.970
What do you guys think?

517
42:51.300 --> 42:52.930
I agree.

518
42:54.130 --> 42:55.930
Me too.

519
42:56.770 --> 42:59.130
I told you I don't like watching football.

520
42:59.770 --> 43:01.770
And you still invited me.

521
43:04.100 --> 43:10.830
Hey, focus on this first. Deal with that later, okay?

522
43:16.170 --> 43:18.330
I know right now

523
43:18.730 --> 43:22.370
all you can think about is getting Aof five goals.

524
43:23.000 --> 43:26.230
But don't forget, safety matters too.

525
43:26.730 --> 43:29.200
I don't have much more to say.

526
43:29.830 --> 43:32.700
I'll be right here watching you succeed.

527
43:32.930 --> 43:33.930
Huddle up!

528
43:39.400 --> 43:42.300
Three, two, one... Thapfah!

529
45:29.200 --> 45:31.930
Don't rush in. Easy.

530
45:51.470 --> 45:53.370
Wait here. I'll be right back.

531
45:53.370 --> 45:55.000
Where to? / Need the toilet.

532
45:57.530 --> 45:59.130
You're leaving me here alone?

533
45:59.130 --> 46:00.370
Yeah, just for a bit.

534
46:22.430 --> 46:24.000
Fuen!

535
46:24.000 --> 46:25.870
What are you doing here?

536
46:25.870 --> 46:28.700
Same as you, checking out the work.

537
46:29.200 --> 46:31.170
No, I mean why are you here?

538
46:31.170 --> 46:32.570
Does Physics know?

539
46:33.200 --> 46:34.770
He'll get the wrong idea.

540
46:35.300 --> 46:36.530
He doesn't.

541
46:38.400 --> 46:40.130
Call him right now.

542
46:41.370 --> 46:43.100
My phone's dead.

543
46:43.100 --> 46:44.270
Use mine?

544
46:44.270 --> 46:45.830
Yeah, can I?

545
46:46.400 --> 46:49.370
Fuen! Tang! You guys came too?

546
46:49.370 --> 46:51.170
Come on, let's take a selfie.

547
46:53.970 --> 46:55.870
Didn't expect to see you here.

548
47:18.600 --> 47:20.830
Break, break, break. Get some water.

549
47:24.500 --> 47:26.300
Aof, just three more goals.

550
47:26.600 --> 47:27.800
You can't do it?

551
47:27.800 --> 47:28.800
Come on, fight.

552
47:28.800 --> 47:29.800
Yeah.

553
47:31.170 --> 47:33.970
I'm not surprised you're all this tired.

554
47:34.430 --> 47:37.730
I told you, what you're doing isn't easy at all.

555
47:37.730 --> 47:39.970
But I believe you can do it.

556
47:41.800 --> 47:44.100
We'll make a new plan for the second half.

557
47:44.930 --> 47:45.900
Fight or not?

558
47:45.900 --> 47:46.830
We'll fight!

559
47:48.400 --> 47:51.100
Here's the thing. Your problem right now

560
47:51.100 --> 47:53.000
is you're all rushing in too much.

561
47:53.000 --> 47:55.170
Time your runs better.

562
47:55.970 --> 47:57.400
Keep your heads.

563
47:57.400 --> 47:58.930
All out in the second half.

564
47:58.930 --> 47:59.930
Fight on!

565
47:59.930 --> 48:01.430
We'll fight! / Good.

566
48:02.030 --> 48:03.300
Take five.

567
48:18.000 --> 48:19.300
What are you guys doing?

568
48:20.930 --> 48:23.730
Nothing. Asking a friend about homework. Thanks a lot.

569
48:23.730 --> 48:24.500
Okay.

570
48:32.530 --> 48:33.700
Why so stressed?

571
50:32.800 --> 50:34.130
That's enough, Aof.

572
50:34.130 --> 50:35.670
I already gave you the chance.

573
50:36.200 --> 50:37.830
It's fine, Chemi.

574
50:37.830 --> 50:39.700
Keep watching me, Chemi.

575
50:43.600 --> 50:45.470
I'm going to make it happen.

576
50:45.470 --> 50:46.670
No, Aof.

577
50:50.100 --> 50:51.700
Look at your leg.

578
50:51.700 --> 50:54.070
What if you push it and it gets worse?

579
50:54.470 --> 50:55.430
I can still do it.

580
51:01.270 --> 51:05.630
Coach, let me take this penalty.

581
51:05.630 --> 51:11.030
I can still play. Trust me, Coach. Please.

582
51:11.630 --> 51:13.630
You're damn stubborn when you want to be.

583
51:13.630 --> 51:16.730
He can actually still play. I'll spray it for him.

584
51:16.730 --> 51:19.470
But if it hurts to put weight on it, stop right away.

585
51:26.670 --> 51:27.600
Careful.

586
53:14.830 --> 53:15.930
Sorry I'm late.

587
53:16.270 --> 53:17.400
The traffic was insane.

588
53:20.270 --> 53:21.930
Why didn't you pick up?

589
53:23.000 --> 53:25.830
Sorry. My phone died.

590
53:29.670 --> 53:31.730
How long are you going to keep lying?

591
53:34.570 --> 53:36.100
It really died.

592
53:42.430 --> 53:45.370
I really hate that we're like this right now.

593
53:50.700 --> 53:52.300
I'm sorry

594
53:54.170 --> 53:56.500
for forcing you to do something you don't like.

595
53:59.370 --> 54:01.000
If this is about today's event,

596
54:01.000 --> 54:03.470
I just went to look. I didn't do anything.

597
54:03.470 --> 54:05.370
Then why didn't you just tell me?

598
54:06.830 --> 54:08.170
Why hide it?

599
54:08.970 --> 54:11.370
I didn't think it was a big deal.

600
54:11.370 --> 54:14.370
And I didn't want you to get the wrong idea.

601
54:16.400 --> 54:18.170
You know what, Fuen?

602
54:18.700 --> 54:20.900
That reason makes no sense at all.

603
54:23.230 --> 54:26.270
I was so damn happy when you said you wanted to go together.

604
54:30.000 --> 54:31.830
What you're doing now...

605
54:34.800 --> 54:37.530
Is it just because you don't know how to say no to me?

606
55:02.430 --> 55:04.200
Think it over again.

607
55:07.600 --> 55:10.470
If you'd rather stay here, just tell me.

608
55:16.270 --> 55:17.830
You don't have to come with me.

609
55:25.130 --> 55:26.600
It's your life, Fuen.

610
55:28.100 --> 55:33.730
♪ Something has begun, and it's getting complicated ♪

611
55:33.730 --> 55:39.000
♪ There's more to it than that ♪

612
55:39.000 --> 55:47.730
♪ I can't find the answer ♪

613
55:49.800 --> 55:55.400
♪ If I'd known this was all the road we had ♪

614
55:55.400 --> 56:00.300
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

615
56:00.300 --> 56:06.530
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

616
56:06.530 --> 56:11.670
♪ We'll never get to love each other again ♪

617
56:15.730 --> 56:21.570
♪ You and I were never meant to be ♪

618
56:25.270 --> 56:27.830
"Can you promise you won't let... Chemi get hurt? (Physics)"

619
56:27.830 --> 56:29.700
"I promise. (Aof)"

620
56:29.700 --> 56:31.270
"I'll wait till you're ready. (Aof)"

621
56:31.270 --> 56:33.070
"After the match. But win it for us"

622
56:33.070 --> 56:34.730
"and score at least five. (Chemi)"

623
56:34.730 --> 56:37.170
"What, Phoodin, in love? No, son, you're in M.6."

624
56:37.170 --> 56:39.530
"No love yet. Wait till university. (Din's Mom)"

625
56:39.970 --> 56:42.670
I don't know what will happen to us from here.

626
56:42.670 --> 56:45.670
This is the last time. I don't want to get hurt again.

627
56:46.700 --> 56:48.730
Aof, take good care of him.

628
56:48.730 --> 56:49.830
Yes, Mom.

629
56:54.770 --> 56:55.670
Hi, Mom.

630
56:55.670 --> 56:57.270
Is Physics home yet?

631
56:57.270 --> 56:58.270
He's not home yet.

632
56:58.270 --> 56:59.670
Didn't you two meet up?

633
57:01.030 --> 57:02.470
How is it? Tasty?

634
57:02.470 --> 57:03.530
It's good.

635
57:03.530 --> 57:05.870
I can feed myself. I'm almost done.

636
57:05.870 --> 57:08.370
Your hands hold the book, your eyes read it.

637
57:08.370 --> 57:10.200
As for your mouth, I'll feed you.

638
57:10.700 --> 57:11.800
Star!

639
57:11.930 --> 57:14.100
Hey! / What?

640
57:15.500 --> 57:16.730
Why are you running away?
